    "display_title": "chore(ci): a spec's parent and milestone follow their items (spec 40 step 5)",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "chore/github-sync-parents-and-milestones-follow-items",
    "head_commit_message": "chore(ci): a spec's parent and milestone follow their items (spec 40 step 5)\n\ngithub-sync now closes a spec's parent when all its steps are closed (as\ncompleted if any step completed, else not planned) and reopens it when a\nstep opens; a `Spec NN: <title>` milestone closes when nothing in it is\nopen and reopens when something is. A parent with no steps and any other\nmilestone are left alone. Every sync run applies the rule from its own\nlisting plus its writes; a new `issues: [closed, reopened]` trigger applies\nit to the changed issue's parent and milestone only, creating nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jd2DwhZv6LSyNbMT4YwHU3",
    "head_sha": "61405d49b29fcdfa113bf7eb72774213cf494019",
